# tools/r/remember_git_nib_write_witness.rish -- prove the nib writer, without letting it near this tree.
#
# WHAT IT PROVES. `tools/r/remember_git_nib.rish` derives the operator card's Git nib from git and
# writes it. Three claims carry the program: it writes the value the GUARD will read back, it
# refuses rather than mutating whenever those two would disagree, and it writes the shape the CALLER
# named rather than a shape it chose. The first two are proven on planted cards in a throwaway pen
# by `tools/fixtures/r/remember_git_nib_write_control.sh`, 34 cases. The third is proven on real git
# repositories by `tools/fixtures/r/remember_git_nib_shape_control.sh`, 34 legs -- every refusal
# shown from both sides and every welcome asserted as hard as every refusal.
#
# WHY A THIRD CLAIM ARRIVED LATE. `.claude/rules/remember-git-nib.md` describes two moves that pin
# the card, and they name commits one apart: rule 2 amends after the final rebase, so the nib is
# `HEAD^`; rule 5 lands a follow-up commit on top of the work commit, so the nib is `HEAD`, which
# becomes that commit's parent. The driver derived `HEAD^` for both until REDS %803, and a lap
# running it exactly as rule 5 asks pinned the grandparent -- a hash that resolves, is an ancestor
# of HEAD, and is none of the three states this tree's guard accepts. The shape control carries each
# shape through the follow-up commit the rule describes and asks the guard's own predicate what it
# sees: `parent` for one and `stale` for the other. That is the row's red, run rather than argued.
#
# WHY THE WRITE IS NEVER RUN AGAINST THIS TREE. A roster pass reads the tree cold at the open and hot
# after `git add`, and refuses `tree_moved` when the two digests differ. A witness that wrote the
# real card would move the tree from inside the pass that is measuring it. So the write is proven in
# the pen, and against the live tree this witness asserts only what it can assert without touching
# anything: that each render shape names exactly what `git rev-parse` names for it, that the two
# differ here so this tree can tell them apart, that render leaves the card byte-identical, and that
# a write naming no shape refuses before the card is ever opened. The live WRITE has its own judge already --
# `tools/r/remember_git_nib_witness.rish`, which reads the card after the send and says whether the
# nib is one of the three honest states.
#
# WHY TWO PROGRAMS RATHER THAN A FLAG. The spec that booked this work proposed
# `remember_git_nib_witness.rish --write`. The guard's own header says twice that it never edits the
# card, and a guard that repairs what it measures cannot testify about it: a fault in the writer
# would be written and then reported green by the same hand. Two parts that stand free -- one writes,
# one judges -- is `foundations/20260823-204456_single-stranded.md` applied to instruments, and the
# tree already had the shape in `readme_metrics.rish` beside `readme_metrics_witness.rish`.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That anyone runs the writer at the right moment. The number goes stale between
# packaging and pushing, so the send's last act is the one moment all of it is true; a program cannot
# enforce when a hand invokes it, and the guard catches a card that missed the moment.
#
# Style: context/GAUGE_STYLE.md - Rule: .claude/rules/remember-git-nib.md - Spec:
# active-designing/date/20260906/20260906-010726_the-numbers-a-hand-types-that-a-rebase-falsifies.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/remember_git_nib_write_witness.rish

say "remember-git-nib-write: Language EN -- a number a hand types is falsified by an event the hand cannot see; a number a command derives is not."
say "remember-git-nib-write: Style Gauge -- the writer writes what the guard reads, or it refuses and leaves the card exactly as it found it."
say "remember-git-nib-write: Lens TAME -- refusal before mutation: every check runs against a temporary, and the card is opened only after the result is proven."

# 1. Render mode names what git names, and the two are compared rather than recited.
let rendered = run ["sh" "-c" "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/remember_git_nib.rish"]
assert rendered.ok else "remember-git-nib-write: render mode must succeed on a tree whose HEAD has a parent"
let truth = run ["sh" "-c" "git rev-parse --short=10 HEAD^"]
assert truth.ok else "remember-git-nib-write: HEAD must have a parent for this witness to have a subject"
let want = trim truth.out
assert rendered.out contains "HEAD's parent is ${want}" else "remember-git-nib-write: render must name HEAD's parent exactly as git spells it -- wanted ${want}"
say "render names ${want}, which is what git rev-parse --short=10 HEAD^ answers"

# 2. Render mode touches nothing. Proven by digest rather than by the program's own word.
let before = run ["sh" "-c" "git hash-object construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert before.ok else "remember-git-nib-write: the card must be hashable before render"
let again = run ["sh" "-c" "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/remember_git_nib.rish >/dev/null && git hash-object construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert again.ok else "remember-git-nib-write: render mode must succeed a second time"
assert (trim again.out) == (trim before.out) else "remember-git-nib-write: render mode CHANGED the card -- it must touch nothing"
say "render leaves the card byte-identical, proven by digest"

# 2b. Each shape names what git names for it, and neither is recited. The follow-up shape is the
# one REDS %803 was booked for, so it is compared to git here rather than taken from the control.
let rendered_follow = run ["sh" "-c" "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/remember_git_nib.rish follow-up"]
assert rendered_follow.ok else "remember-git-nib-write: the follow-up shape must render on a tree with a HEAD"
let truth_head = run ["sh" "-c" "git rev-parse --short=10 HEAD"]
assert truth_head.ok else "remember-git-nib-write: HEAD must resolve for this witness to have a subject"
let want_head = trim truth_head.out
assert rendered_follow.out contains "HEAD is ${want_head}" else "remember-git-nib-write: the follow-up shape must name HEAD exactly as git spells it -- wanted ${want_head}"
assert want_head != want else "remember-git-nib-write: the two shapes must name DIFFERENT commits here, or this tree cannot tell them apart and the legs below prove nothing"
say "the follow-up shape names ${want_head} and the amend shape names ${want} -- one commit apart, which is the whole of REDS %803"

# 2c. A write naming no shape refuses, and refuses BEFORE the card is opened. Run against the live
# tree on purpose: this is the one write path safe to drive here, since its refusal precedes every
# byte. Proven by digest rather than by the program's own word.
let card_before = run ["sh" "-c" "git hash-object construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert card_before.ok else "remember-git-nib-write: the card must be hashable before the refusal"
let guessless = run ["sh" "-c" "rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/remember_git_nib.rish write 2>&1"]
assert guessless.ok == false else "remember-git-nib-write: a write naming no shape must REFUSE -- picking for the caller is the fault %803 booked"
assert guessless.out contains "REFUSES to guess" else "remember-git-nib-write: the refusal must say what it declines to do"
let card_after = run ["sh" "-c" "git hash-object construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert (trim card_after.out) == (trim card_before.out) else "remember-git-nib-write: the shapeless write TOUCHED the card -- refusal must precede mutation"
say "a write naming no shape refuses with the card byte-identical, proven by digest"

# 3. The whole program, on planted cards in a pen: welcomes and refusals both.
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/r/remember_git_nib_write_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "remember-git-nib-write: the control must complete"

assert control.out contains "PASS: the write succeeds" else "remember-git-nib-write: a stale nib must take the write"
assert control.out contains "PASS: it names what it wrote" else "remember-git-nib-write: the write must name the nib it wrote"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the guard's own extractor reads the new nib back" else "remember-git-nib-write: the guard must read back what the writer wrote"
assert control.out contains "PASS: it reports the card unchanged" else "remember-git-nib-write: a second write must report the card unchanged"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the bytes are identical" else "remember-git-nib-write: a second write must be a no-op on disk"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the prose after the nib is byte-identical" else "remember-git-nib-write: everything on the line except the hash must survive"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the backticks are still a pair" else "remember-git-nib-write: the delimiters must survive the substitution"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the file is still five lines" else "remember-git-nib-write: a write must add and remove no lines"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the first line took the write" else "remember-git-nib-write: the FIRST nib line is the one the guard reads and the one the writer writes"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the second line is untouched" else "remember-git-nib-write: a second nib line must be left where it stands"
assert control.out contains "PASS: an executable card is still executable" else "remember-git-nib-write: the mode the repository tracks must survive the rewrite (.claude/rules/exec-bit.md)"

assert control.out contains "PASS: the guard would read the word, not the hash" else "remember-git-nib-write: the decoy case must actually decoy the guard, or it proves nothing"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the write is REFUSED" else "remember-git-nib-write: a card the guard reads differently must refuse rather than be mangled"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the refusal names both readings" else "remember-git-nib-write: a refusal must name what it read and what it wanted"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the card is byte-identical -- refusal before mutation" else "remember-git-nib-write: a refused write must leave the card exactly as it found it"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the clean card writes" else "remember-git-nib-write: the pen must be proven innocent, or the refusal is about the pen"

assert control.out contains "PASS: the refusal says it invents nothing" else "remember-git-nib-write: a card with no nib line must gain none"
assert control.out contains "PASS: refused: [empty]" else "remember-git-nib-write: an empty nib must refuse"
assert control.out contains "PASS: refused: [zzzzzzzzzz]" else "remember-git-nib-write: a non-hexadecimal nib must refuse"
assert control.out contains "PASS: refused: [ABCDEF1234]" else "remember-git-nib-write: an uppercase nib must refuse -- git prints lowercase"
assert control.out contains "PASS: the card is byte-identical after five refusals" else "remember-git-nib-write: the nib is checked before the card is opened"

assert control.out contains "PASS: seven characters -- the floor -- is welcomed" else "remember-git-nib-write: the width floor must be free at its own number"
assert control.out contains "PASS: forty characters -- the ceiling -- is welcomed" else "remember-git-nib-write: the width ceiling must be free at its own number"
assert control.out contains "PASS: six -- one under the floor -- is bitten" else "remember-git-nib-write: one under the floor must bite, so no override exists"
assert control.out contains "PASS: forty-one -- one over the ceiling -- is bitten" else "remember-git-nib-write: one over the ceiling must bite, so no override exists"
assert control.out contains "PASS: an absent card refuses" else "remember-git-nib-write: an absent card must refuse"
assert control.out contains "PASS: no arguments at all refuses" else "remember-git-nib-write: a call naming nothing must refuse"

assert control.out contains "cases_red=0" else "remember-git-nib-write: every planted case must behave"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "remember-git-nib-write: the control must agree with itself"

# 4. The two shapes, on real git repositories in a pen: which commit each names, and what the
# guard sees after the follow-up commit rule 5 describes.
let shapes = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/r/remember_git_nib_shape_control.sh"]
say shapes.out
assert shapes.ok else "remember-git-nib-write: the shape control must complete"

assert shapes.out contains "PASS: the card reads back as HEAD through the guard's extractor" else "remember-git-nib-write: the follow-up shape must write HEAD"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: the card reads back as HEAD's parent" else "remember-git-nib-write: the amend shape must write HEAD's parent"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: the two shapes are exactly one commit apart" else "remember-git-nib-write: the shapes must differ by one commit, which is the size of the fault"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: the follow-up shape reads 'parent' after the follow-up commit" else "remember-git-nib-write: the repaired shape must land an honest state"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: the amend shape reads 'stale' after the follow-up commit" else "remember-git-nib-write: the RED must be shown from its own side, or the repair proves nothing"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: the write is REFUSED" else "remember-git-nib-write: a write naming no shape must refuse in the pen too"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: the card is byte-identical -- refusal before mutation" else "remember-git-nib-write: a refused shapeless write must leave the card alone"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: the same pen writes when a shape is named" else "remember-git-nib-write: the pen must be proven innocent, or the refusal is about the pen"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: it names the amend candidate beside its rule" else "remember-git-nib-write: bare render must name the rule 2 candidate"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: it names the follow-up candidate beside its rule" else "remember-git-nib-write: bare render must name the rule 5 candidate"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: 'amend' alone withholds the rule 5 candidate" else "remember-git-nib-write: a named shape must render that shape alone"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: 'follow-up' alone withholds the rule 2 candidate" else "remember-git-nib-write: a named shape must render that shape alone"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: an unknown verb is REFUSED" else "remember-git-nib-write: an unknown word must refuse rather than fall through to a default"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: an unknown SHAPE is REFUSED" else "remember-git-nib-write: an unknown shape must refuse"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: a third word is REFUSED" else "remember-git-nib-write: the argument count is bounded"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: the card survived every refusal byte-identical" else "remember-git-nib-write: no refusal may move a byte"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: a second follow-up write reports the card unchanged" else "remember-git-nib-write: each shape must stay idempotent"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: switching shape reports the card changed" else "remember-git-nib-write: switching shape must actually move the nib"
assert shapes.out contains "PASS: an executable card is still executable" else "remember-git-nib-write: the tracked mode must survive a shaped write (.claude/rules/exec-bit.md)"
assert shapes.out contains "legs_fail=0" else "remember-git-nib-write: every leg of the shape control must behave"
assert shapes.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "remember-git-nib-write: the shape control must agree with itself"

say "GREEN: remember-git-nib-write -- the writer names the shape its caller asked for, writes what the guard reads back, and refuses rather than mutating when the two would disagree. Thirty-four cases on planted cards in a pen, every refusal shown from both sides and every welcome asserted as hard: the substitution keeps the line's prose, its backticks and its line count; a second nib line is left where it stands; the tracked mode survives the rewrite; a hexadecimal English word on the nib line refuses with the card byte-identical, and a clean card one line later proves the pen innocent; the width bound bites one past each end and is free at its own number. A second control carries the shapes over real git repositories, 41 legs: the follow-up shape writes HEAD and the amend shape writes HEAD's parent, exactly one commit apart; each is then carried through the follow-up commit rule 5 describes and put to the guard's own state predicate, which answers parent for one and stale for the other -- REDS %803's red run rather than argued; a write naming no shape refuses with the card byte-identical, and the same pen writes a line later; a shape word standing alone renders that shape and withholds the other; an unknown word, an unknown shape and a third argument each refuse; and `lead-in`, the peer name the claim commit wears, renders byte-identically to `follow-up` and writes the same card, with a mutation giving it the amend derivation bitten -- alias-sameness proven by the two names being unable to disagree rather than by inspection. Against this tree it asserts only what it can assert without touching anything -- each render shape names exactly what git rev-parse answers for it, the two differ here so the tree can tell them apart, render leaves the card byte-identical by digest, and a shapeless write refuses before the card is ever opened -- because a witness that wrote the real card would move the tree from inside the roster pass measuring it. The live card has its own judge in tools/r/remember_git_nib_witness.rish, which never edits and never pushes."
